    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d718">

                <pb facs="0869" n="851" xml:id="pg851"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24522/4–246: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in
                    Ecuador</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-02T15:00:00-05:00">April 2, 1946—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>127. Galo Plaza yesterday presented Dept with note formally requesting withdrawal
                    from Galápagos at earliest possible moment.</p>
                <p>Dept asking War and Navy to set date. You will be kept advised of
                        developments.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d718-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d718-f1" n="38" xml:id="d718-f1-content">
                <p>The Department advised the Ambassador in telegram 135, April 4, 1946, 7 p.m.,
                    that July 1, 1946, was the date set for complete withdrawal
                    (811.24522/4–446).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
